// expect-error: NITPICK-DERIVE-005
// expect-error: NITPICK-DERIVE-005
//
// THE TWO OF THE SEVEN THAT ARE REFUSED RATHER THAN GENERATED — under their own
// code since 1.0.8, because they are names `#[derive]` knows, not unknown ones.
//
// `Hash` FOLDS BYTES with FNV-1a (D-123). The premise this file carried — that
// nothing exposes a `string`'s bytes to Nitpick source — has been false since
// 0.7.8 (`s.ptr[i]`); what is missing is the generator, owed at 1.0.9.
//
// `Ord` ON AN ENUM means comparing a variant's tag, which `enum =>! int32` has
// read since 0.8.0; the generator that writes that comparison is owed at 1.0.9.
//
// Both refuse HERE rather than generating code that fails to type-check, because a
// diagnostic inside generated code points at a line nobody wrote.
mod:not_generated;

#[derive(Hash)]
struct:A = { int32:x; };

#[derive(Ord)]
enum:E = { ONE; TWO; };

func:main = int32(cstring[]:_~argv) { exit 0i32; };
